<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42229" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saetōsus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēt-</span></b> ), a, um, adj.
		saeta, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of coarse hairs</i> or <i>bristles</i>, <i>bristly</i>, <i>setous</i> (mostly
				<b>poet.</b>; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">villosus, pilosus): aper,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 7, 29</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">setosa membra (of the sailors of Ulysses,
					transformed into swine by Circe),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					Epod. 17, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aures tauri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 45, 70, § 181</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 5, 61</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pectus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 2,
					8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verbera,</span>”
				<i>made of goats' hair</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					4, 1, 25</span></i>
			.</div>
